    "https://employment.ku.edu/jobs/faculty/instructor-political-science/34049br": {
      "title": "Instructor | Political Science",
      "description": "Job Posting - Instructor | Political Science Job Posting | Work at KU Skip to main content The University of Kansas MENU link to menu page THE UNIVERSITY of KANSAS Work at KU myKU Email Canvas Enroll & Pay Jayhawk GPS Close Search this unit Start search Submit Search Main navigation Home Jobs Select to follow link Faculty, Lecturers, and Academic Staff Staff Students Application Status How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Benefits Culture at KU Why KU? Contact Us Info for Prospective Students Current Students Alumni Degree Programs myKU Email Canvas Enroll & Pay Jayhawk GPS THE UNIVERSITY of KANSAS University of Kansas logo Work at KU Menu link to menu page Search this unit Start search Submit Search Home All Jobs Faculty, Instructional, and Academic Staff Jobs Job Posting Short Instructor | Political Science Position Overview The Department of Political Science is currently hiring for instructors to teach virtual courses at the undergraduate level in the Intelligence & National Security Studies program. The instructor is an instructional, adjunct faculty position that is not eligible for tenure or promotion in rank. This is a term appointment for the Spring 2027 semester. Renewal will be based upon unit needs and funding as well as performance that meets expectations, not to exceed two continuous semesters. This position is subject to a collective bargaining agreement between The University of Kansas and United Academics, United Academics of KU, AAUP, or AFT.  UAKU is the exclusive representative. As the State of Kansas is a right to work state, you have the right to be a member or not be a member of a union without fear of personal or professional repercussions. The successful candidate must be eligible to work in the U.S. prior to the start date of the position. Due to complex state employment laws, the University of Kansas may be unable to hire fully remote workers for this position outside of Kansas. Specifically, we cannot currently offer employment to candidates residing in the following states:  California, Delaware, Idaho, and Minnesota. We appreciate your understanding and invite interested individuals from eligible states to apply. Job Description 100% Instructional Duties: As an instructor for the university, primary duties and responsibilities include: teaching in a specific field, developing course materials, developing and managing syllabi, creating lectures and assignments, grading student work, advising students and holding office hours. All instructors are expected to collaborate with colleagues, be current in the field, and are required to adhere to departmental, school/college and university policies and procedures Attend required instructor training, as required by the department, and provided by the Center for Teaching Excellence The Lecturer should be available for reasonable appointments if a student requests a meeting either in person or virtual. Adhere to departmental, college, and university policies Required Qualifications For Instruction of Undergraduate-Level Courses: MA in discipline or relevant field OR BA in discipline & 5 years of relevant experience. Relevant experience in the Intelligence & National security sector. Preferred Qualifications PhD in Political Science. Evidence of prior college-level teaching experience in Political Science or specific course of interest. Additional Candidate Instructions A complete application will include a letter of application (see below), a CV/resume detailing specific subject areas the applicant is qualified to teach and/or develop, and the names and contact information for three professional references. A sample syllabus for a similar course is recommended. Please address the following areas in your letter of application: What experience do you have with the development and management of an undergraduate course syllabus? If you have not developed a college-level syllabus, please describe any comparable experience developing training programs, educational materials, curricula, or structured learning content. What experience do you have with creating undergraduate lectures and assignments? If applicable, describe related experience designing training sessions, presentations, workshops, instructional materials, or professional development programs. What experience do you have with grading work and advising college students? Candidates without direct college teaching experience are encouraged to discuss relevant experience mentoring, coaching, supervising, evaluating performance, or providing feedback to learners, trainees, or professional staff. What is your overall teaching strategy? Please describe your approach to facilitating learning, engaging students, communicating complex concepts, assessing understanding, and supporting learner success in an academic or professional training environment. Contact Information to Applicants Ashley Urban , Department of Political Science ashleylu@ku.edu Advertised Salary Range $6,562.50 per 3 hour online/asynchronous course Application Review Begins Monday November 9, 2026 Anticipated Start Date Monday November 23, 2026 Apply to Job Search Jobs Search all jobs Start search Posting Information Posting ID: &nbsp34049BR Department: &nbspPolitical Science Primary Campus: &nbspUniversity of Kansas Lawrence Campus Assignment: &nbspTelework Reg/Temp: &nbspTemporary Employee Class: &nbspF-Faculty Review Begins: &nbsp09-Nov-2026 Apply to this job Existing Candidate Login Jobs by Type Faculty, Instructional, and Academic Staff Staff Students Other Employment at KU Athletics KU Dining & Memorial Unions Endowment Alumni KUMC Off-Campus Student Employment Related Links Employment Posters Human Resources Immigration Related Notices Civil Rights and Title IX KUMC Human Resources Carruth O'Leary Hall 1246 West Campus Road, Room 101 Lawrence, Kansas 66045-7521 employ@ku.edu 785-864-4946 facebook instagram twitter youtube linkedin Human Resources New Hires at KU Benefits Visit KU KU Admissions KU Endowment KU News KU Events KU Careers KU Alumni Nondiscrimination statement Accessibility | Website support | CMS login © 2026 The University of Kansas The University of Kansas prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, status as a veteran, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in the university's programs and activities. Retaliation is also prohibited by university policy. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the nondiscrimination policies and procedures and is the Title IX Coordinator for all KU and KUMC campuses: Associate Vice Chancellor for the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX, civilrights@ku.edu , Room 1082, Dole Human Development Center, 1000 Sunnyside Avenue, Lawrence, KS 66045, 785-864-6414 , 711 TTY. Reports can be submitted by contacting the Title IX Coordinator as provided herein or using the Title IX online report form and complaints can be submitted with the Title IX Coordinator or using the Title IX online complaint form . The University of Kansas is a public institution governed by the Kansas Board of Regents."
